  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\nShowers will a few embedded thunderstorms continue to move across the\narea. While more robust activity is generally progressive, it has\nalso been quite proficient given warm rain processes in a very moist\nenvironment. Most of these showers and storms will be passing east of\nthe forecast area towards daybreak. Flood watch continues. Cannot\nrule out a few spotty showers developing this afternoon.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2)\nMid level trough extending from Hudson Bay to the southern\nAppalachians will become deeper as a substantial short wave drops\nthrough the Great Lakes into the upper Ohio Valley on Saturday. This\nwill push a cold front through the area Saturday afternoon and\nevening. Atmosphere is forecast to become moderately unstable, but\nbetter shear is lagging the instability. If this remains the case,\nthen storm organization will be limited.",
